---
import Marketing from '../layouts/Marketing.astro';
---
<Marketing
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms for using Total Recall and theo, in plain language: what the service is, what you own, what we promise, and what we ask of you."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(32px,4.6vw,52px);margin:10px 0 0">Terms of service.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin:18px 0 0">
        Plain language, because you should actually read the terms of a product that remembers
        your life. Using Total Recall or theo means you agree to these.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-top:40px;display:grid;gap:28px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65">
        <p style="color:var(--muted,#666);margin:0">Effective date: July 12, 2026</p>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">The service</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Total Recall sets up and operates software that gives you a private, single-owner
            knowledge base (your "brain") and an AI assistant (theo) that uses it. The brain runs
            in accounts you own: your database provider, your hosting provider, and your AI
            provider accounts. We provide the software, the setup, the app you use it through,
            and support.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Your data and your accounts</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Your content belongs to you, full stop. It lives in infrastructure under your own
            logins, and our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> describes the little we hold
            ourselves. You are responsible for the third-party accounts the service runs on
            (database, hosting, AI providers), including their costs and their terms. If you
            stop paying those providers, your brain stops running; that is between you and them,
            though we will help you handle it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Payment</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Total Recall is a paid service. Prices are shown before you commit, and connected
            integrations (like our Slack app) are included in your subscription rather than
            billed separately. Third-party infrastructure costs in your own accounts are yours
            and are estimated honestly during setup.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Acceptable use</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            Connect only accounts and data you have the right to connect. Do not use the service
            to violate laws, other people's privacy, or the terms of the platforms you connect
            (Slack, Google, Notion, and the rest). One brain belongs to one person; do not resell
            or share access to yours.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">What we promise, and what we do not</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            We work to keep the service reliable, honest about its limits, and safe by
            architecture. But the service is provided "as is": we do not warrant that it will be
            uninterrupted or error-free, and AI assistants can be wrong, so verify anything
            consequential before acting on it. To the maximum extent the law allows, our
            liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the
            claim. Nothing here limits liability where the law does not allow it to be limited.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Ending things</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            You can stop any time: export your data, tear down your infrastructure (our guides
            cover both), and cancel. We may suspend or end service for breach of these terms,
            with notice where practical. Because your data is in your accounts, ending the
            relationship never holds your memory hostage.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 style="margin:0 0 8px">Changes and contact</h2>
          <p style="margin:0">
            If these terms change materially, we will update this page and its effective date and
            let active customers know. Questions:
            <a href="mailto:support@totalrecallhq.com">support@totalrecallhq.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Marketing>
